### Step 1: Add scroll detection
Add after the toggleFollow function:
```javascript
function handleScroll() {
    if (!isFollowing) return;

    const threshold = 50;
    const isAtBottom = logContainer.scrollHeight - logContainer.scrollTop - logContainer.clientHeight < threshold;

    if (!isAtBottom) {
        // User scrolled up, disable follow mode
        const followBtn = document.getElementById('follow-btn');
        const followIcon = document.getElementById('follow-icon');
        const followText = document.getElementById('follow-text');

        isFollowing = false;
        followBtn.classList.remove('active');
        followIcon.textContent = '⏸️';
        followText.textContent = 'Follow';
    }
}
```

### Step 2: Register scroll event listener
Add at the end of the script (before closing script tag):
```javascript
logContainer.addEventListener('scroll', handleScroll);
```

## Notes
- Uses 50px threshold to avoid false positives from minor scroll adjustments
- Only checks when currently in follow mode (optimization)
- This matches GitHub/GitLab behavior where scrolling up pauses auto-scroll

## Acceptance Criteria
- Scrolling up while in follow mode automatically disables it
- Button updates to show paused state
- Small scrolls near bottom don't trigger disable (50px threshold)

